{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>Then Moses separated.</b> 'Az' is an expression of song, like ״אז ישיר משה״. For when they heard that the Holy One, blessed be He, said ״ולארץ לא יכופר לדם כי אם בדם שופכו״, they said: What? One who killed unintentionally should be killed? When Moses told them its remedy — to flee to cities of refuge — then they said song. And that is what people say: one who eats the cooked dish knows its taste. So too Moses: when he killed the Egyptian and fled, he knew the punishment of killers — to flee." "<b>Eastward, sunward.</b> All murderers flee there. Adam the first, who decreed death upon the children of the world, fled to the east, as it is said: ״וישכן מקדם לגן עדן״ etc. Cain fled to the east, as it is said: ״ויצא קין מלפני ה׳ וישב בארץ נוד קדמת עדן״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:32.914419571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}